.TH CDLOCKER 1 "June 2026" "ColDog Locker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdlocker \- manage encrypted ColDog Locker directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdlocker
.br
.B cdlocker gui
.br
.B cdlocker tui
.br
.B cdlocker terminal
.br
.B cdlocker new
.I name
.RB [ --path
.IR parent ]
.RB [ --password
.IR password ]
.br
.B cdlocker lock
.I name
.RB [ --password
.IR password ]
.br
.B cdlocker unlock
.I name
.RB [ --password
.IR password ]
.br
.B cdlocker list
.RB [ --locked | --unlocked ]
.br
.B cdlocker status
.I name
.br
.B cdlocker verify
.I name
.br
.B cdlocker change-password
.I name
.RB [ --old-password
.I password
.B --new-password
.IR password ]
.br
.B cdlocker remove
.I name
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --delete ]
.br
.B cdlocker settings
.RI [ key
.RI [ value ]]
.br
.B cdlocker db-info
.br
.B cdlocker db-vacuum
.br
.B cdlocker update
.RB [ --download ]
.br
.B cdlocker help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B cdlocker --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cdlocker
creates and manages password-protected locker directories. A locker is stored as
a normal directory while it is unlocked. Locking verifies the locker password,
encrypts files recursively, renames the directory with a leading dot, marks it
hidden or system where supported, and updates the local locker database.
Unlocking reverses that operation.
.PP
Locker metadata is stored in a per-user SQLite database. Settings and logs are
stored under the per-user local app data directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Launch the graphical interface.
.TP
.BR tui ", " terminal
Launch the terminal user interface.
.TP
.BI "new " name
Create a locker. Use
.B --path
to choose the parent directory. Use
.B --password
for automation.
.TP
.BI "lock " name
Encrypt and hide a locker. Prompts for a password unless
.B --password
is supplied.
.TP
.BI "unlock " name
Decrypt and unhide a locker. Prompts for a password unless
.B --password
is supplied.
.TP
.B list
Print all lockers. Use
.B --locked
or
.B --unlocked
to filter.
.TP
.BI "status " name
Print state, path, GUID, timestamps, and content counts.
.TP
.BI "verify " name
Check that the locker directory and metadata are consistent.
.TP
.BI "change-password " name
Change a locker password. The locker must be unlocked.
.TP
.BI "remove " name
Remove a locker from metadata. Use
.B --force
to skip confirmation. Use
.B --delete
to delete the directory contents too.
.TP
.B settings
Show all settings, show one setting, or update one setting.
.TP
.B db-info
Print SQLite database information.
.TP
.B db-vacuum
Optimize the SQLite database.
.TP
.B update
Check for releases. Release notes are printed automatically when available. Use
.B --download
to download, verify, and start a matching installer.
.TP
.B help
Show help.
.TP
.BR --version ", " -v
Show version and build information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--path " parent
Parent directory for a new locker. The locker directory is created as
.IR parent/name .
.TP
.BI "--password " password
Supply a password on the command line. This is useful for automation but can
expose secrets through shell history, scripts, logs, or process listings.
.TP
.BI "--old-password " password
Supply the current password for
.BR change-password .
Must be used with
.BR --new-password .
.TP
.BI "--new-password " password
Supply the replacement password for
.BR change-password .
Must be used with
.BR --old-password .
.TP
.B --locked
Show only locked lockers in
.BR list .
.TP
.B --unlocked
Show only unlocked lockers in
.BR list .
.TP
.B --force
Skip removal confirmation.
.TP
.B --delete
Delete the locker directory when removing the locker.
.TP
.B --download
Download, verify, and start a matching update installer when available.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker/settings.json
Application settings on many Unix-like systems.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker/lockers.db
Locker metadata database on many Unix-like systems.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ColDog Studios/ColDog Locker/logs/
Application logs on many Unix-like systems.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error.
.TP
.B 2
Update available but no downloadable installer is available for the current
platform.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
cdlocker new MyLocker
cdlocker new Taxes --path "$HOME/Private"
cdlocker lock MyLocker
cdlocker unlock MyLocker
cdlocker list --locked
cdlocker verify MyLocker
cdlocker settings update-channel stable
cdlocker update
.EE
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Use strong, unique passwords and keep backups. ColDog Locker cannot recover
forgotten passwords. Avoid command-line password options for interactive use.
System paths, drive roots, profile roots, and top-level user folders are blocked
from becoming lockers.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.I https://github.com/ColDog-Studios/ColDog-Locker/tree/main/docs
